trong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c9-t1-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>, which they depend on for navigation</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Toxins</strong></p><p>Poisons from <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c9-t1-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> or animals are commonly consumed by whales</p><p>e.g. Cape Cod (1988) – whales were killed by saxitoxin</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Accidental Strandings</strong></p><p>Animals may follow prey ashore, e.g. Thurston (1995)</p><p>Unlikely because the majority of animals were not <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c9-t1-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> when they stranded</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Human Activity</strong></p><p><span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c9-t1-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> from military tests are linked to some recent strandings</p><p>The Bahamas (2000) stranding was unusual because the whales</p><ul><li>were all <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c9-t1-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>were not in a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c9-t1-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Group Behaviour</strong></p><ul><li>More strandings in the most <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c9-t1-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> species of whales</li><li>1994 dolphin stranding – only the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c9-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> was ill</li></ul><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Further Reading</strong></p><p><em>Marine Mammals Ashore</em> (Connor) – gives information about stranding <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c9-t1-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-09-academic-listening-test-1-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c9-t1-l-q1","part_id":"en-c9-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c9-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"answering the phone/answering phone/answer the phone/answer phone","correct_answer_variants":["answering the phone","answering phone","answer the phone","answer phone"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3164262_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c9-t1-l-q2","part_id":"en-c9-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c9-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"Hillsdunne Road","correct_answer_variants":["Hillsdunne Road"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3164262_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c9-